    {
      "title": "I-T dept extends corporate tax audit, ITR filing deadlines by three weeks",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/finance/news/i-t-dept-extends-corporate-tax-audit-itr-filing-deadlines-by-three-weeks-126092800954_1.html",
      "description": "The Income Tax Department on Monday extended by 21 days the due date for ITR filing and submission of audit report by corporates for assessment year 2026-27.\nAccordingly, corporates will now have to file income tax return for AY'27 by November 21, instead of October 31. Similarly, the due date for tax audit report submission has been extended from September 30 to October 21.\nIn a statement, the Central Board of Direct Taxes (CBDT) said the due dates for both the compliances have been extended.\nTax practitioners have been demanding an extension of the corporate statutory audit report and ITR filing deadline from September 30 citing compressed audit window following the August 31 deadline for filing ITR in non-audit cases.\nNangia & Co LLP Senior Partner Amit Agarwal, said the extension shows that the CBDT has taken cognisance of the genuine challenges being faced by taxpayers and tax professionals during the current compliance cycle.\n\"The additional 21 days will provide much-needed",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-28T12:32:00"
    }
  ]
